    {
      "id": "planning_debug_guided_tour_not_working_runtime_setup_overlay",
      "label": "Runtime Setup Overlay (#runtime-setup-overlay)",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\marsh\\Documents\\LecturePack-worktrees\\release-polish\\.planning\\debug\\guided-tour-not-working.md",
      "source_location": "## Root Cause Analysis",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "The guided tour overlay was originally nested inside #runtime-setup-overlay, which carries the `hidden` attribute on every healthy launch. Because CSS parents with [hidden] hide all children regardless of inner style changes, the overlay could not be shown; the fix moved it into the #app root container."
    },
    {
      "id": "planning_debug_guided_tour_not_working_css_hidden_behavior",
      "label": "CSS [hidden] Parent Hides Children",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\marsh\\Documents\\LecturePack-worktrees\\release-polish\\.planning\\debug\\guided-tour-not-working.md",
      "source_location": "## Root Cause Analysis",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Mechanism: a parent container with [hidden] hides all child elements regardless of inner style changes such as display:flex, so toggling child overlay.hidden=false alone has no visible effect while the parent remains hidden."
    },
    {
      "id": "planning_debug_guided_tour_not_working_guided_tour_class",
      "label": "GuidedTour (show/hide)",
      "file_type": "code",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\marsh\\Documents\\LecturePack-worktrees\\release-polish\\.planning\\debug\\guided-tour-not-working.md",
      "source_location": "## Fix Applied",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "GuidedTour.show() and hide() were updated to toggle overlay.style.display between 'flex' and 'none' alongside overlay.hidden, so the overlay renders independently of parent visibility."
    },
